<li class="matrx-list-item"><strong class="matrx-strong">Mechanism:</strong> The absence of anticoagulant triggers the natural coagulation cascade. Thrombin converts fibrinogen into a polymerized│ Major Payor Stance (Aetna, Cigna, BCBS, UHC): "Experimental/Unproven" <strong class="matrx-strong">3D fibrin matrix</strong> that physically traps platelets, leukocytes, and circulating stem cells [7].</li>
<li class="matrx-list-item"><strong class="matrx-strong">i   │ +─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+ │ Primary Billing Codes: CPT 0232T | HCPCS G0460 / G0465 / P9020         │ +────────────────-PRF (Injectable PRF):</strong> Centrifuged at ultra-low G-forces for short durations, yielding─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+ │ Coverage Exceptions: CMS NCD 270.3 (Diabetic Wounds) a liquid preparation that remains unclotted for ~15–20 minutes before forming a dynamic fibrin clot inside the target | Workers' Comp    │ +─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+ │ Tax &amp; Financing Strategies: HSA/FSA Eligibility tissue [7].</li>
<li class="matrx-list-item"><strong class="matrx-strong">Sustained Release Advantage:</strong> Unlike standard PRP, which releases >90% of its growth factor | CareCredit / Prosper │ +─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+</li>
</ul>
</div></div></section>"
`;

